{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>If you lend money.</b> If HaShem has given you wealth so that you are able to lend to the poor, and he mentioned this passage because the poor are like the stranger, the orphan, and the widow, and he called the poor 'my people,' for the pious do not seek wealth in this world. And the witness is Elijah and Elisha, who did not wish to accept the gift of Naaman, also Samuel the Ramatite." "<b>And the meaning of 'with you.'</b> That it is in the place where you dwell." "<b>You shall not be to him as a creditor.</b> That he should show you favor on account of your benefit. And he said <b>you shall set.</b> For the lender and the scribe and the witnesses all transgress."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:28.299719973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}